Subject: select-v2: a button trigger that takes its own attributes

What: the trigger renders as Kobalte's default <button> instead of a div (the value
wrapper becomes a span so the button's content stays phrasing content), and
`triggerProps` spreads onto it: an `id` for a label's `for`, an `aria-label`,
a test hook. The trigger sheet resets the button's UA font, color, margin and
text alignment.
Why: a div trigger is not labelable, so a <label for> next to it focuses nothing,
and the root's attributes never reach the element that carries the accessible
name and the expanded state.

